Bowers et al. describe **Stitch** differently: it is a **deductive refactoring / library-learning** approach that learns abstractions by running “**CTS after a single step of version space rewriting and then probabilistically re-ranking the results**.” They conclude that “**running Stitch on top of a deductive rewrite system reduces the expressivity gap**,” and that it is related to “**deductive refactoring and library learning systems**.”

So, in short:
- **EC2**: joint learning of a DSL and a neural search model.
- **Stitch**: deductive library learning via rewrite-based refactoring plus ranking of candidate abstractions.
